<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>CNN Fear &amp; Greed vs SPY and QQQ</title><style>body{background:#0b1320;color:#e7effb;font:16px/1.5 system-ui;margin:0}main{max-width:1180px;margin:auto;padding:20px}h2{font-size:25px}h3{font-size:18px}a{color:#56d6c0}summary{font-weight:650;cursor:pointer}.eyebrow{font-size:12px;color:#a6b7ce}</style><style id="dashboard-dark-theme">:root{color-scheme:dark}body{background:#0b1320;color:#e7effb}::selection{background:#345d8c;color:#fff}select,input,button{color-scheme:dark}a:focus-visible,button:focus-visible,select:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #79adff;outline-offset:3px}</style><nav aria-label="Wiki navigation" style="background:#101c2e;color:#a6b7ce;border-bottom:1px solid #2d4059;padding:10px 24px;font:14px Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif"><a href="../index.html" style="color:#79adff;text-decoration:none">← Wiki dashboards</a><span style="margin:0 12px">/</span><a href="index.html" style="color:#79adff;text-decoration:none">Sentiment Radar</a><span style="margin:0 12px">/</span><a href="http://DS-CAP-33:8080/dashboards/#sentiment-radar" style="color:#79adff;text-decoration:none">Main dashboards</a></nav><main><div id="weekly-level-explorer"><p>Opening the next-week study…</p></div><script>/* Shared, offline conditional-return explorer: dashboard and standalone study. */
(function(global){
'use strict';
const colors={SPY:'#79adff',QQQ:'#56d6c0'},valid=x=>typeof x==='number'&&Number.isFinite(x);
const f=(x,n=2,sign=false)=>valid(x)?(sign&&x>0?'+':'')+x.toLocaleString('en-US',{minimumFractionDigits:n,maximumFractionDigits:n}):'—';
const pct=x=>valid(x)?f(x,2,true)+'%':'—',esc=s=>String(s??'').replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]));
const scale=(a,b,c,d)=>v=>c+(v-a)/(b-a||1)*(d-c);
const interval=(r,key='mean_ci95',unit='%')=>r[key]?f(r[key][0],2,true)+unit+' to '+f(r[key][1],2,true)+unit:'Insufficient sample';
const label=c=>c===0?'0–<5':c===100?'95–100':`${c-5}–<${c+5}`;
const css=`.wl{font:16px/1.5 'Segoe UI',Arial,sans-serif;color:#e7effb}.wl *{box-sizing:border-box}.wl h1,.wl h2,.wl h3,.wl p{margin:0}.wl h1{font-size:28px;letter-spacing:-.7px;line-height:1.25}.wl h2{font-size:20px;letter-spacing:-.3px}.wl h3{font-size:17px}.wl p{font-size:14px;color:#a6b7ce}.wl-head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:18px;align-items:end;margin:0 0 18px}.wl-head p{margin-top:6px}.wl-controls{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;margin-bottom:20px}.wl label{font-size:14px;color:#a6b7ce}.wl select,.wl button.wl-btn{font:14px 'Segoe UI',sans-serif;color:#e7effb;background:#142033;border:1px solid #2d4059;border-radius:7px;padding:9px 11px;max-width:100%}.wl button,.wl select{cursor:pointer}.wl button:focus-visible,.wl select:focus-visible,.wl [tabindex]:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #5796ff;outline-offset:3px}.wl-summary{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:15px;margin:0 0 20px}.wl-tile{border:1px solid #2d4059;border-radius:12px;background:#142033;padding:16px 18px;text-align:left;color:#e7effb}.wl-tile[aria-pressed=true]{border-color:#79adff;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px #79adff}.wl-tile strong{font-size:29px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.8px}.wl-tile small{display:block;color:#a6b7ce;font-size:12px}.wl-tile p{margin-top:8px;font-size:14px}.wl-tile b{font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.wl-card{background:#142033;border:1px solid #2d4059;border-radius:14px;overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:20px}.wl-card-head{padding:19px 22px 12px;display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:space-between;align-items:start}.wl-card-head p{margin-top:4px}.wl-card-body{padding:0 22px 20px}.wl-chart{overflow:auto}.wl svg{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.wl svg text{font:14px 'Segoe UI',Arial,sans-serif;fill:#a6b7ce}.wl-legend{display:flex;gap:18px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:13px;color:#a6b7ce}.wl-legend i{display:inline-block;width:10px;height:10px;border-radius:2px;margin-right:5px}.wl-note{font-size:12px;color:#a6b7ce;padding:12px 22px;border-top:1px solid #2b3d55}.wl-baseline{background:#101c2e;color:#e7effb;border-radius:10px;padding:15px 20px;display:flex;gap:26px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:20px;font-size:14px}.wl-baseline b{font-size:18px}.wl-split{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.wl-stats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:14px;padding-top:10px}.wl-stats strong{display:block;font-size:23px;letter-spacing:-.6px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.wl-stats span{display:block;font-size:12px;color:#a6b7ce}.wl-up{color:#56d6c0}.wl-down{color:#f295ad}.wl-callout{background:#1b3150;padding:14px 17px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:15px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6}.wl-callout.warn{background:#392f21;color:#efc77f}.wl-scroll{overflow:auto}.wl table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px}.wl th,.wl td{padding:11px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid #2b3d55;text-align:right;white-space:nowrap;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.wl th{font-size:12px;background:#101c2e;color:#a6b7ce}.wl th:first-child,.wl td:first-child{text-align:left}.wl .wl-empty{padding:28px 0;color:#a6b7ce;font-size:15px}.wl details{margin-top:15px}.wl summary{cursor:pointer;font-size:14px;font-weight:600}.wl details p{margin-top:10px;line-height:1.7}.wl-link{color:#79adff;text-decoration:none}.wl-small{font-size:12px;color:#a6b7ce}.wl-gap{margin-bottom:20px}.wl-group:hover .wl-hover,.wl-group:focus .wl-hover{fill:#1b3150;fill-opacity:.55}.wl-group{cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:850px){.wl-summary{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.wl-split{grid-template-columns:1fr}.wl-head{align-items:start;flex-direction:column}}@media(max-width:560px){.wl-summary{gap:10px}.wl-tile{padding:12px}.wl-tile strong{font-size:24px}.wl-card-head,.wl-card-body{padding-left:15px;padding-right:15px}.wl-chart>svg{min-width:650px}.wl-stats{gap:8px}.wl-stats strong{font-size:20px}}`;

function stats(data,state,t,c=state.level){return data.results[t][state.timing].groups[state.sample+'_'+c];}
function barChart(data,state){const centers=state.sample==='cross'?data.meta.thresholds:data.meta.centers;const w=1080,h=370,l=66,r=24,t=26,b=75,all=centers.flatMap(c=>['SPY','QQQ'].map(t=>stats(data,state,t,c))),vals=all.flatMap(r=>[r.mean_pct,...(r.mean_ci95||[])]).filter(valid);let lo=Math.min(0,...vals),hi=Math.max(0,...vals);const pad=(hi-lo||1)*.13;lo-=pad;hi+=pad;const y=scale(lo,hi,h-b,t),step=(w-l-r)/centers.length;let body='';for(let k=0;k<5;k++){const v=lo+(hi-lo)*k/4;body+=`<line x1="${l}" x2="${w-r}" y1="${y(v)}" y2="${y(v)}" stroke="#2b3d55"/><text x="${l-10}" y="${y(v)+5}" text-anchor="end">${f(v,1)}%</text>`;}body+=`<line x1="${l}" x2="${w-r}" y1="${y(0)}" y2="${y(0)}" stroke="#9cafc4"/>`;
 centers.forEach((c,i)=>{const xx=l+step*(i+.5),sr=stats(data,state,'SPY',c),selected=c===state.level;body+=`<g class="wl-group" role="button" tabindex="0" data-wl-level="${c}" aria-label="Explore CNN ${c}; ${sr.n} observations"><rect class="wl-hover" x="${xx-step*.48}" y="${t}" width="${step*.96}" height="${h-b-t}" rx="5" fill="${selected?'#1b3150':'#142033'}" fill-opacity="${selected?1:0}"/>`;
 for(const [ticker,offset] of [['SPY',-12],['QQQ',12]]){const s=stats(data,state,ticker,c),col=colors[ticker],cx=xx+offset;if(!s.n)continue;const mean=s.mean_pct;body+=`<rect x="${cx-8}" y="${y(Math.max(0,mean))}" width="16" height="${Math.max(1,Math.abs(y(mean)-y(0)))}" rx="2" fill="${col}" opacity="${s.n<20?.45:.9}"/>`;if(s.mean_ci95){const [a,b]=s.mean_ci95;body+=`<line x1="${cx}" x2="${cx}" y1="${y(a)}" y2="${y(b)}" stroke="${col}" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="${cx-4}" x2="${cx+4}" y1="${y(a)}" y2="${y(a)}" stroke="${col}"/><line x1="${cx-4}" x2="${cx+4}" y1="${y(b)}" y2="${y(b)}" stroke="${col}"/>`;}body+=`<title>${ticker}, CNN ${c}: mean ${pct(mean)}, median ${pct(s.median_pct)}, up ${f(s.positive_pct,1)}%, n=${s.n}</title>`;}
 body+=`<text x="${xx}" y="${h-b+24}" text-anchor="middle" style="fill:${selected?'#79adff':'#e7effb'};font-weight:600">${state.sample==='cross'?(c<=30?'≤':'≥'):''}${c}</text><text x="${xx}" y="${h-b+44}" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:12px">${sr.n?'n='+sr.n:'No data'}</text></g>`;});body+=`<text x="${w/2}" y="${h-7}" text-anchor="middle">${state.sample==='cross'?'CNN threshold crossed · selected windows do not overlap':'CNN level · fixed ±5-point bands'}</text>`;return `<svg viewBox="0 0 ${w} ${h}" role="img" aria-label="Mean next-week returns after CNN levels, with uncertainty">${body}</svg>`;}
function distribution(data,state){const a=stats(data,state,'SPY'),b=stats(data,state,'QQQ'),rr=[a,b];if(!a.n)return '<div class="wl-empty">No observations in this sample. The maximum CNN reading was '+f(data.meta.observed_max,2)+'.</div>';const vals=rr.flatMap(r=>[r.p10_pct,r.p90_pct,0]).filter(valid),lo=Math.min(...vals)-.3,hi=Math.max(...vals)+.3,w=760,h=205,l=65,r=24,x=scale(lo,hi,l,w-r);let body='';for(let k=0;k<5;k++){const v=lo+(hi-lo)*k/4;body+=`<line x1="${x(v)}" x2="${x(v)}" y1="20" y2="155" stroke="#2b3d55"/><text x="${x(v)}" y="185" text-anchor="middle">${f(v,1)}%</text>`;}body+=`<line x1="${x(0)}" x2="${x(0)}" y1="20" y2="155" stroke="#9eb2cf" stroke-dasharray="4 3"/>`;['SPY','QQQ'].forEach((t,i)=>{const s=rr[i],yy=58+i*65;body+=`<text x="10" y="${yy+5}" style="fill:${colors[t]};font-weight:700">${t}</text><line x1="${x(s.p10_pct)}" x2="${x(s.p90_pct)}" y1="${yy}" y2="${yy}" stroke="${colors[t]}" stroke-width="12" stroke-opacity=".2" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="${x(s.median_pct)}" cy="${yy}" r="6" fill="${colors[t]}"/><path d="M${x(s.mean_pct)},${yy-8} l6,8 l-6,8 l-6,-8 Z" fill="#142033" stroke="${colors[t]}" stroke-width="2"/><text x="${x(s.p10_pct)}" y="${yy-17}" text-anchor="middle">${pct(s.p10_pct)}</text><text x="${x(s.p90_pct)}" y="${yy-17}" text-anchor="middle">${pct(s.p90_pct)}</text>`;});return `<svg viewBox="0 0 ${w} ${h}" role="img" aria-label="10th to 90th percentile of realised returns, median and mean">${body}</svg>`;}
function card(data,state,t){const s=stats(data,state,t);return `<article class="wl-card"><div class="wl-card-head"><h2 style="color:${colors[t]}">${t}</h2><span class="wl-small">${s.n} ${state.sample==='all'?'daily readings':'separate windows'}${s.n>0&&s.n<20?' · small sample':''}</span></div><div class="wl-card-body">${!s.n?'<div class="wl-empty">No estimate: this level was not observed in the sample.</div>':`<div class="wl-stats"><div><strong class="${s.mean_pct>=0?'wl-up':'wl-down'}">${pct(s.mean_pct)}</strong><span>Mean next-week return</span></div><div><strong>${pct(s.median_pct)}</strong><span>Median next-week return</span></div><div><strong>${f(s.positive_pct,1)}%</strong><span>Weeks with a positive return</span></div></div><div class="wl-callout">Against all eligible days: <b>${f(s.excess_vs_all_pp,2,true)} pp</b> in mean return.<br>95% interval for this difference: <b>${interval(s,'excess_ci95',' pp')}</b>.</div><p style="margin-top:12px">Return-mean interval: ${interval(s)}. Negative weeks: ${f(s.negative_pct,1)}%; unchanged: ${f(s.flat_pct,1)}%.</p>`}</div></article>`;}
function mount(root,data,initial={}){const state={timing:'close',sample:'cross',level:30,...initial};function render(){if(state.sample==='cross'&&!data.meta.thresholds.includes(state.level))state.level=30;const baseline=data.results.SPY[state.timing].baseline,baseQ=data.results.QQQ[state.timing].baseline,selected=stats(data,state,'SPY'),keys=state.sample==='cross'?data.meta.thresholds:data.meta.centers;if(!keys.includes(state.level))state.level=30;root.innerHTML=`<style>${css}</style><div class="wl"><div class="wl-head"><div><h1>What follows an approach to sentiment extremes?</h1><p>New zone entries · next 5 US trading sessions · ${data.meta.start} to ${data.meta.end} · CNN history and Bloomberg total returns.</p></div><button class="wl-btn" data-action="export">Export selected observations ↓</button></div><div class="wl-controls"><label>Sample <select data-control="sample"><option value="cross">Extreme approaches · new threshold crossings</option><option value="episode">Diagnostic · first entries into all bands</option><option value="all">Diagnostic · every daily reading</option></select></label><label>Return timing <select data-control="timing"><option value="close">Reading-day close → 5 sessions later</option><option value="delayed">Next-session close → hold 5 sessions</option></select></label></div><div class="wl-summary">${(data.meta.primary_thresholds||[20,30,70,80]).map(c=>{const a=stats(data,state,'SPY',c),b=stats(data,state,'QQQ',c);return `<button class="wl-tile" data-wl-level="${c}" aria-pressed="${state.level===c}"><strong>${state.sample==='cross'?(c<=30?'≤':'≥'):''}${c}<span style="font-size:14px;color:#a6b7ce"> / 100</span></strong><small>${state.sample==='cross'?'New extreme-zone entry':'Band '+label(c)} · ${a.n} observations</small><p>${a.n?`SPY <b>${pct(a.mean_pct)}</b><br>QQQ <b>${pct(b.mean_pct)}</b>`:'No observations<br>No extrapolation'}</p></button>`;}).join('')}</div><div class="wl-baseline"><span>Normal 5-session performance<br><small>All eligible daily readings · ${baseline.n} observations</small></span><span>SPY <b>${pct(baseline.mean_pct)}</b> · up ${f(baseline.positive_pct,1)}%</span><span>QQQ <b>${pct(baseQ.mean_pct)}</b> · up ${f(baseQ.positive_pct,1)}%</span></div><article class="wl-card"><div class="wl-card-head"><div><h2>${state.sample==='cross'?'Following week after entering an extreme zone':'Return in the following week, by starting level'}</h2><p>Click a level to inspect the distribution, hit rate and sample size.</p></div><div class="wl-legend"><span><i style="background:${colors.SPY}"></i>SPY</span><span><i style="background:${colors.QQQ}"></i>QQQ</span><span>Whiskers: 95% interval of the mean</span></div></div><div class="wl-card-body wl-chart">${barChart(data,state)}</div><div class="wl-note">${state.sample==='all'?'Counts include consecutive days and overlapping future weeks. Use first entries to avoid repeatedly counting the same band visit.':'New entries/crossings are selected chronologically; a new holding window cannot start before the prior selected window ends within the same band/threshold. Days remaining inside a zone are not new events. A move through 30 then 20 (or 70 then 80) is a deeper extreme in the same phase; do not add these counts as independent episodes.'} Pale bars: fewer than 20 observations. Intervals suppressed below 10 observations.</div></article><div class="wl-head"><div><h2>${state.sample==='cross'?'Crossing '+(state.level<=30?'down to ≤':'up to ≥')+state.level:'Near '+state.level+' · band '+label(state.level)}</h2><p>${selected.n?'Observed outcomes, not a forecast for the next occurrence.':'No history supports an estimate at this level.'}</p></div><label>Inspect level <select data-control="level">${keys.map(c=>`<option value="${c}">${c} ${state.sample==='cross'?'threshold':'· '+label(c)}</option>`).join('')}</select></label></div><div class="wl-split">${card(data,state,'SPY')}${card(data,state,'QQQ')}</div><article class="wl-card"><div class="wl-card-head"><div><h2>How wide was the range of outcomes?</h2><p>Central 80% of realised 5-session returns. These are outcome percentiles, not confidence intervals.</p></div><div class="wl-legend"><span>● Median</span><span>◇ Mean</span><span>Line: 10th–90th percentile</span></div></div><div class="wl-card-body wl-chart">${distribution(data,state)}</div></article><article class="wl-card"><div class="wl-card-head"><div><h2>Does the selected level behave the same across years?</h2><p>Exclude outcomes that cross a year-end. Small annual cells are descriptive only.</p></div></div><div class="wl-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>n</th><th>SPY mean</th><th>SPY up</th><th>QQQ mean</th><th>QQQ up</th></tr></thead><tbody>${selected.yearly.map((s,i)=>{const q=stats(data,state,'QQQ').yearly[i];return `<tr><td>${s.year}</td><td>${s.n}</td><td>${pct(s.mean_pct)}</td><td>${s.n?f(s.positive_pct,1)+'%':'—'}</td><td>${pct(q.mean_pct)}</td><td>${q.n?f(q.positive_pct,1)+'%':'—'}</td></tr>`;}).join('')}</tbody></table></div></article><div class="wl-callout warn wl-gap">A positive conditional return is not enough: compare it with the market's normal positive drift. Check whether the advantage over normal market drift survives uncertainty and the delayed-entry control. ${data.results.SPY[state.timing].groups.all_90.n===0?'No observations near 90; sample maximum '+f(data.meta.observed_max,2)+'.':''}</div><details><summary>Timing, definitions and sources</summary><p><b>Retained history is reused; changing a view does not collect new data.</b></p><p><b>Five sessions means one trading week</b>, not five calendar days or a fixed Monday–Friday week. Default return: total-return index at t+5 divided by its reading-date close at t, minus one. This is a descriptive event study; the historical CNN file does not establish availability before that close. The delayed-entry control enters at t+1 close and exits at t+6 close.</p><p>Near 30 means 25 ≤ CNN &lt;35. Other centered bands use the same ±5 points; only the last band includes 100. First entries can arrive from either side. Directed crossings are different: prior CNN above 20/30, current at or below it; or prior below 70/80/90, current at or above it. The 20/30 and 70/80 cutoffs are operational watch zones, distinct from CNN’s official category boundaries. A missing prior reading cannot establish a new entry.</p><p>Intervals: 1,000 circular moving-block resamples, 20 ETF sessions per block, retaining missing CNN dates on the original calendar. Not adjusted for comparisons across bands. History is retrospective and may be revised; no causal or executable-strategy claim. Gross total returns include dividends and exclude trading costs.</p><p><a class="wl-link" href="https://www.cnn.com/markets/fear-and-greed" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CNN official index ↗</a> · ETF series: Bloomberg Desktop API, TOT_RETURN_INDEX_GROSS_DVDS. Data through ${data.meta.end}; last primary signal with a full outcome: ${data.meta.signal_end}. Current day and all earlier-than-2021 history are outside this sample.</p></details></div>`;
root.querySelectorAll('[data-control]').forEach(e=>{e.value=state[e.dataset.control];e.onchange=()=>{state[e.dataset.control]=e.dataset.control==='level'?+e.value:e.value;if(state.sample==='cross'&&!data.meta.thresholds.includes(state.level))state.level=30;render();};});root.querySelectorAll('[data-wl-level]').forEach(e=>{e.onclick=()=>{state.level=+e.dataset.wlLevel;render();};e.onkeydown=ev=>{if(ev.key==='Enter'||ev.key===' '){ev.preventDefault();state.level=+e.dataset.wlLevel;render();}};});root.querySelector('[data-action="export"]').onclick=()=>{const key=state.sample+'_'+state.level,rows=[['ticker','signal_date','cnn_level','entry_date','exit_date','total_return_5_sessions_pct','timing','sample']];for(const t of ['SPY','QQQ'])for(const r of data.observations[t][state.timing])if(r.groups.includes(key))rows.push([t,r.date,r.fg,r.entry_date,r.exit_date,r.return_pct,state.timing,key]);const csv=rows.map(r=>r.map(v=>'"'+String(v).replaceAll('"','""')+'"').join(',')).join('\r\n'),url=URL.createObjectURL(new Blob(['\ufeff'+csv],{type:'text/csv;charset=utf-8'})),a=document.createElement('a');a.href=url;a.download='cnn-'+state.level+'-next-week-'+state.sample+'-'+state.timing+'.csv';a.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(url),1000);};
}render();}
global.WeeklyLevels={mount,barChart,distribution,stats,css};
if(typeof module!=='undefined')module.exports=global.WeeklyLevels;
})(globalThis);
</script><script>(async()=>{try{const b=Uint8Array.from(atob(""),c=>c.charCodeAt(0));const s=new Blob([b]).stream().pipeThrough(new DecompressionStream("gzip"));const d=JSON.parse(await new Response(s).text());WeeklyLevels.mount(document.getElementById("weekly-level-explorer"),d);}catch(e){document.getElementById("weekly-level-explorer").textContent="Open this file in a current Edge, Chrome or Firefox browser. "+e.message;}})();</script><details style="margin-top:32px"><summary>Additional diagnostics: correlations, longer horizons and historical charts</summary><section id="market-study" class="mkt"><style>.mkt{background:#142033;border:1px solid #2d4059;padding:24px;margin:24px 0}.mkt svg{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.mkt svg text{font:12px system-ui;fill:#a6b7ce}.mkt-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.mkt-note{padding:15px;background:#173333;border-left:4px solid #56d6c0}.mkt table{width:100%;font-size:13px;border-collapse:collapse}.mkt th,.mkt td{padding:9px;border-bottom:1px solid #2d4059;white-space:normal;text-align:right}.mkt td:first-child,.mkt th:first-child{text-align:left}.mkt .scroll{overflow:auto}.mkt small{font-size:12px;color:#a6b7ce}.mkt details{margin-top:18px;padding:14px 0;border-top:1px solid #2d4059}.mkt-legend{font-size:13px;display:flex;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap}@media(max-width:850px){.mkt-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.mkt{padding:15px}}</style>
<div class="eyebrow">MARKET STUDY · CNN FEAR &amp; GREED × SPY / QQQ</div><h2>Market conditions versus forward returns</h2>
<p>2021-02-01 to 2026-09-18 · <b>1,414 matched sessions</b> · CNN history and Bloomberg total-return indices. Current day excluded from the study; latest CNN snapshot: <b>33.7/100 · fear</b>, 2026-09-21T21:06:51+00:00.</p>
<div class="mkt-note"><b>Daily change in Fear &amp; Greed versus same-day return:</b> SPY <b>0.63</b> (95% block interval [0.58, 0.68]); QQQ <b>0.59</b> ([0.56, 0.63]).<br><b>Fear &amp; Greed level versus later 20-session return:</b> SPY -0.13; QQQ -0.09. Both confidence intervals include zero. Controlling for momentum and volatility: SPY -0.05, QQQ -0.04. Association with current market conditions does not itself establish standalone timing value.</div>
