<h3>Does today's CNN reading lead future returns?</h3><p>Signal observed on day t; conservative entry at the <b>next session's close</b>, then hold for the stated number of sessions. Positive correlation would favor higher CNN readings; negative correlation is contrarian. These are associations, not a fitted strategy.</p><div class="mkt-legend"><span style="color:#56d6c0">● SPY</span><span style="color:#c8a9f1">● QQQ</span><span style="color:#efb682">● QQQ/SPY ratio</span><span>Dots = Pearson; lines = 95% block-bootstrap intervals</span></div><svg role="img" aria-label="Future-return correlations with 95 percent block intervals" viewBox="0 0 980 300" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><line x1="70" x2="960" y1="228.0" y2="228.0" stroke="#2b3d55"/><text x="62" y="232.0" text-anchor="end">-0.4</text><line x1="70" x2="960" y1="184.0" y2="184.0" stroke="#2b3d55"/><text x="62" y="188.0" text-anchor="end">-0.2</text><line x1="70" x2="960" y1="140.0" y2="140.0" stroke="#8395a0"/><text x="62" y="144.0" text-anchor="end">0.0</text><line x1="70" x2="960" y1="96.0" y2="96.0" stroke="#2b3d55"/><text x="62" y="100.0" text-anchor="end">0.2</text><line x1="70" x2="960" y1="52.0" y2="52.0" stroke="#2b3d55"/><text x="62" y="56.0" text-anchor="end">0.4</text><line x1="157.25" x2="157.25" y1="160.3" y2="139.9" stroke="#56d6c0" stroke-width="3"/><circle cx="157.25" cy="149.7" r="5" fill="#56d6c0"><title>SPY 1 sessions: -0.044; CI -0.092, 0.000</title></circle><text x="181.25" y="282" text-anchor="middle">1 sessions</text><line x1="379.75" x2="379.75" y1="179.4" y2="138.0" stroke="#56d6c0" stroke-width="3"/><circle cx="379.75" cy="156.7" r="5" fill="#56d6c0"><title>SPY 5 sessions: -0.076; CI -0.179, 0.009</title></circle><text x="403.75" y="282" text-anchor="middle">5 sessions</text><line x1="602.25" x2="602.25" y1="212.3" y2="130.2" stroke="#56d6c0" stroke-width="3"/><circle cx="602.25" cy="169.1" r="5" fill="#56d6c0"><title>SPY 20 sessions: -0.132; CI -0.329, 0.044</title></circle><te